; ============================================================================
; RECONSTRUCTED — this file was NOT produced by Cloudflare's "Export" button.
; ============================================================================
;
; Provenance, stated so nobody mistakes this for a genuine export:
;
;   * The record DATA is real. Every RRset below was read back from Cloudflare's
;     DoH JSON API on 2026-08-10 with
;       curl -H 'accept: application/dns-json' \
;         'https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query?name=<name>&type=<TYPE>'
;     and the owner names are the ones the zone's own DNS dashboard lists.
;
;   * The FORMATTING is reconstructed from Cloudflare's public import/export
;     documentation (fully-qualified owner with a trailing dot, an explicit
;     numeric TTL where `1` means "automatic", an explicit `IN` class, one
;     record per line, inline `;` comments appending record attributes). It has
;     NOT been diffed against a byte-for-byte real export, so the BIND subset in
;     ADR-026 §7 remains unverified against genuine Cloudflare output.
;
;   * Two records are SYNTHETIC and marked `; synthetic` inline: the split
;     character-string DKIM TXT (real zones carry one; this zone's DKIM name is
;     a CNAME to the ESP) and the `_sip._tcp` SRV. Both exist so the parser has
;     something to bite on.
;
; The "unsupported constructs" section at the end is deliberate: every row of
; ADR-026 §7's "not supported, and reported rather than ignored" table appears
; there at least once, so a parser test can assert that each one comes back as a
; reported line with a reason rather than being silently dropped.

; --- apex -------------------------------------------------------------------

